n 2,8 contratos. La razón entre observados y esperados es 12,1, con un intervalo de confianza del 95 % de 6,3 a 24,5. En diciembre se adjudicó el 3 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 2 % de todos sus contratos de obras. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 11 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 38.813,50 euros, se adjudicó en septiembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: El hecho de que se adjudiquen contratos cerca del límite no prueba que haya sido un error o que haya habido irregularidad. Puede ser una decisión basada en precios de mercado o necesidades específicas.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1] y [2] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en distintas áreas. Analizar si los contratos de diciembre se relacionan con un plan anual previsto.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 34 minor contracts for works above 37,500 and up to 40,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 2.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 12.1, with a 95% confidence interval of 6.3 to 24.5. December accounts for 3% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 2% of all its works contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 11 different awardees. Contract [1], for 38,813.50 euros, was awarded in September 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The high ratio shows a pattern, but it doesn't prove wrongdoing. Prices near the limit can be due to market rates or budget constraints. Statistical trends don't indicate improper actions by the body or contractors.\nWhat can be checked: Check the contracts' dates and amounts to see if they align with budget needs. Review awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same type of work. Look at December's contracts to see if they follow a different pattern than other months.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_